{
  "name": "razorbill",
  "version": 3,
  "introduced_by": "gannet",
  "notes": "circle: Razorbill, the base of the diving auks. Stands upright on land like a small penguin, legs far back, and sits low on the sea; black above and sharply white below, a deep blade-shaped black bill crossed by a white line (`bill_stripe`) and a fine white line from the bill to the eye (`face_line`). Short narrow wings with a white trailing edge, a short pointed tail. Nests on cliff ledges beside the puffins, circles low off the cliffs and dives for fish. Puffin, murrelet and the like inherit it: recolour `bill`, `bill_stripe`, `belly`, `face_line` or swap the bill ops.",
